        promptText: "Some people think that technology has made our lives too complex and that the solution is to lead a simpler life without technology. Others, however, believe that technology is making our lives easier.\n\nDiscuss both these views and give your own opinion.",
        modelAnswer: "Introduction:\nIn contemporary society, the rapid advancement of technology has profoundly impacted daily life. While some individuals argue that these innovations have needlessly complicated our existence and advocate for a return to a simpler, technology-free lifestyle, others contend that modern devices have significantly eased our burdens. This essay will examine both perspectives before concluding that technology's benefits far outweigh its complexities.\n\nBody Paragraph 1:\nThose who advocate for a simpler, less technologically dependent life often point to the stress and distraction caused by modern devices. The ubiquity of smartphones and the internet means that people are constantly connected, leading to an inability to switch off from work or social pressures. This constant connectivity can result in mental fatigue and a loss of meaningful, face-to-face interactions. Furthermore, the rapid pace of technological change requires individuals to constantly learn new systems and interfaces, which can be overwhelming, particularly for older generations. Consequently, retreating to a lifestyle free from such digital intrusions is seen as a way to reclaim peace of mind and foster deeper human connections.\n\nBody Paragraph 2:\nConversely, the opposing view emphasizes the unparalleled convenience and efficiency that technology introduces into our lives. From a practical standpoint, household appliances like washing machines and dishwashers have drastically reduced the time spent on domestic chores. In the professional sphere, computers and the internet have revolutionized communication and information retrieval, allowing for global collaboration and instantaneous access to vast repositories of knowledge. Medical technology, too, has advanced leaps and bounds, simplifying the diagnosis and treatment of diseases, thereby extending life expectancy and improving life quality.\n\nBody Paragraph 3:\nIn my opinion, while it is true that technology can introduce new layers of complexity and stress if not managed properly, abandoning it entirely is an extreme and regressive solution. The conveniences and advancements brought about by technological progress are simply too valuable to discard. Instead of rejecting technology, individuals should focus on establishing healthy boundaries and utilizing digital tools intentionally.\n\nConclusion:\nIn conclusion, although the continuous evolution of technology can create challenges and a sense of complexity, its contributions to easing domestic burdens, enhancing global communication, and advancing medical science are undeniable. A balanced approach to technology usage is far more practical than striving for an entirely simplified, tech-free life.\n\nHow to Plan Your Answer:\n• Step 1: Analyze the Prompt: Identify the specific topic and the exact question type (e.g., Do you agree? Discuss both sides?).\n• Step 2: Formulate Your Stance: Decide on your clear overall opinion or thesis right away. (e.g., \"In conclusion, although the continuous evolution of technology can create challenges and a sense of complexity, its contributions to easing domestic burdens, enhancing global communication, and advancing medical science are undeniable.\")\n• Step 3: Outline Your Body Paragraphs: Pick one main supporting idea for each paragraph.\n  - Paragraph 1 Idea: Those who advocate for a simpler, less technologically dependent life often point to the stress and distraction caused by modern devices.\n  - Paragraph 2 Idea: Conversely, the opposing view emphasizes the unparalleled convenience and efficiency that technology introduces into our lives.\n  - Paragraph 3 Idea: In my opinion, while it is true that technology can introduce new layers of complexity and stress if not managed properly, abandoning it entirely is an extreme and regressive solution.\n• Step 4: Think of Examples: Before writing, quickly jot down one real-world example or logical reason to support each of your paragraph ideas.\n\n• Points to Note for this Question:\n  - Connecting to the Prompt: The prompt focuses on the issue: \"Some people think that technology has made our lives too complex and that the solution is to lead a simpler life without technology. Others, however, believe that technology is making our lives easier\". The model answer tackles this by exploring \"Those who advocate for a simpler, less technologically dependent life often point to the stress and distraction caused by modern devices.\" in the first body paragraph and \"Conversely, the opposing view emphasizes the unparalleled convenience and efficiency that technology introduces into our lives.\" in the second.\n  - How to Come Up With This: To generate the body ideas yourself, always ask 'What is the strongest logical consequence of the prompt's theme?' This leads directly to the core thesis: although the continuous evolution of technology can create challenges and a sense of complexity, its contributions to easing domestic burdens, enhancing global communication, and advancing medical science are undeniable.\n  - Band 9 Strategy: Notice how the essay logically connects every supporting example back to the central theme of the prompt. This proves your position is completely consistent."
