        promptText: "Today, more and more people are delaying having children until they are older.\n\nWhat are the reasons for this trend? Do you think this is a positive or negative development?",
        modelAnswer: "Introduction:\nIn recent decades, there has been a noticeable demographic shift, with an increasing number of individuals and couples opting to start families later in life. This essay will explore the socioeconomic reasons driving this trend and argue that, despite some biological risks, it is largely a positive development for both families and society.\n\nBody Paragraph 1:\nThe primary driver behind the delay in parenthood is the changing nature of modern career and educational trajectories. Today, both men and women are pursuing higher education and striving to establish secure careers before taking on the immense financial and temporal responsibilities of raising a child. In many contemporary economies, achieving financial stability requires years of dedication, making early parenthood economically daunting. Furthermore, the rising cost of living, particularly housing and childcare, forces many prospective parents to wait until they have accumulated sufficient savings. Another contributing factor is the shift in societal norms; there is less pressure to conform to traditional timelines, allowing individuals to prioritize personal growth and travel in their twenties.\n\nBody Paragraph 2:\nIn my view, this trend towards older parenthood is primarily positive. When individuals wait until they are older to have children, they are generally more financially secure, which allows them to provide a more stable and enriching environment for their offspring. They are less likely to struggle with the costs of education, healthcare, and extracurricular activities. Additionally, older parents often possess a higher degree of emotional maturity and life experience. Having had the time to fulfill personal ambitions, they may experience less resentment and be more patient and dedicated to the child-rearing process.\n\nBody Paragraph 3:\nWhile it is true that advanced maternal and paternal age can pose certain medical risks, modern advancements in healthcare and prenatal screening have significantly mitigated these dangers.\n\nConclusion:\nIn conclusion, the decision to delay parenthood is a logical response to the financial and educational demands of the modern world. Because it generally results in children being raised in more secure, financially stable, and emotionally mature households, I consider it a highly positive societal development.\n\nHow to Plan Your Answer:\n• Step 1: Analyze the Prompt: Identify the specific topic and the exact question type (e.g., Do you agree? Discuss both sides?).\n• Step 2: Formulate Your Stance: Decide on your clear overall opinion or thesis right away. (e.g., \"In conclusion, the decision to delay parenthood is a logical response to the financial and educational demands of the modern world.\")\n• Step 3: Outline Your Body Paragraphs: Pick one main supporting idea for each paragraph.\n  - Paragraph 1 Idea: The primary driver behind the delay in parenthood is the changing nature of modern career and educational trajectories.\n  - Paragraph 2 Idea: In my view, this trend towards older parenthood is primarily positive.\n  - Paragraph 3 Idea: While it is true that advanced maternal and paternal age can pose certain medical risks, modern advancements in healthcare and prenatal screening have significantly mitigated these dangers.\n• Step 4: Think of Examples: Before writing, quickly jot down one real-world example or logical reason to support each of your paragraph ideas.\n\n• Points to Note for this Question:\n  - Connecting to the Prompt: The prompt focuses on the issue: \"Today, more and more people are delaying having children until they are older\". The model answer tackles this by exploring \"The primary driver behind the delay in parenthood is the changing nature of modern career and educational trajectories.\" in the first body paragraph and \"In my view, this trend towards older parenthood is primarily positive.\" in the second.\n  - How to Come Up With This: To generate the body ideas yourself, always ask 'What is the strongest logical consequence of the prompt's theme?' This leads directly to the core thesis: the decision to delay parenthood is a logical response to the financial and educational demands of the modern world.\n  - Band 9 Strategy: Notice how the essay logically connects every supporting example back to the central theme of the prompt. This proves your position is completely consistent."
